Chapter 16
Corporate culture, the code of conduct, and core values
ثقافة الشركة ومدونة السلوك والقيم الجوهرية
Chapter 15 ended by saying that controls fail where people do not believe in them. This chapter is about what people do believe, where that comes from, and what a company can do to shape it.
Three instruments do the work and the exam treats them separately. Corporate culture, which is what actually happens; the code of conduct, which is what the company has written down; and core values, which are the few commitments the code and the culture are both supposed to express. The fourth outcome asks what all of this is worth, which is a fair question and one that has better answers than it usually receives.
Figure F816-01 is your map.
Figure F816-01. Chapter 16 roadmap: culture, the code, the core values, and what they are worth.
