Case-style practice: the values exercise
Orontes's board has approved six corporate values and a twenty-four page code, with acknowledgement at 100 per cent. In the same two years: one concern was raised through the reporting line, about car parking; a senior manager left quietly after expense irregularities while a warehouse employee was dismissed for taking stock worth 400; a two-month gap in the inventory reconciliation went unreported; and the quarterly result has landed within 1 per cent of forecast eleven times.
Required. Say what the evidence indicates, what you would do about the code and the values, and what you would measure instead of acknowledgement rates. Under 350 words.
Answers and explanations are at the end of the chapter.
Answers and explanations
